CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --array-rf
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
When c is 0 the thread writes x, and a[1] keeps 0, so the assertion fails.
A read-from that took the conditional update as made wherever p points would
always find 5 at a[1] and report SUCCESSFUL: a missed bug.

The condition is stated twice: in the update and in the guard of the step
symex emits it under, which the write's exec symbol includes. Dropping it from
the selection alone therefore changes nothing here; it is kept so that the
decomposition does not depend on that.

See array_rf_conditional_update_taken for the other direction.
